# SpeakEasy — Knowledge Graph Schema

**Owner:** Tiana
**Layer:** Progress & Intelligence
**Sprint:** 3 (Weeks 5–6)
**Database:** Neo4j Aura (free tier)

---

## Overview

This file defines the Knowledge Graph (KG) layer for SpeakEasy. The KG is the backbone of all personalization — it stores every user's session history, question-by-question scores, and weak areas. Sahel's RL agent reads from this graph to decide which exercises to prioritize next, and Tiana's dashboard reads from it to surface progress over time.

**Sprint 3 schema change:** scoring and weak-phoneme tracking moved from the whole session down to each individual question/exercise response. Previously a session had one `overall_score` and the user's weak phonemes were computed by averaging scores across a whole session. Now every question a user answers within a session — each one an `Attempt` node — gets its own score and its own weak-phoneme flags, so a teammate's code can compare how a user did question-to-question within a single session and pick the next exercise to better match their actual weak points, instead of only reacting after a whole session is over.

