## Graph Schema

### Node types

| Node | Properties | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `User` | `user_id`, `phone_number`, `age_group`, `native_language`, `created_at` | One node per user, keyed by WhatsApp number |
| `Track` | `track_id`, `name` | Fixed therapy tracks — seeded once at setup |
| `Session` | `session_id`, `overall_score`, `duration_seconds`, `speech_rate_wpm`, `filler_total`, `embedding`, `timestamp` | One node per practice session — a container for its `Attempt`s. The score/rate/filler/embedding fields here are legacy, from before question-level tracking existed; new code should read those off `Attempt` instead (see below) |
| `Attempt` | `attempt_id`, `user_id`, `session_id`, `exercise_id`, `subcategory`, `transcription`, `speech_rate_wpm`, `filler_words`, `filler_total`, `total_duration_s`, `score`, `scoring_method`, `scoring_details`, `weak_phonemes`, `embedding`, `timestamp` | **New in Sprint 3.** One node per question/exercise response within a session — this is where score, weak phonemes, and embeddings actually live now |
| `Phoneme` | `symbol` | A speech sound e.g. `/r/`, `/th/`, `/s/` |
| `Score` | `value`, `timestamp` | **Legacy** — a float 0–1 score for one phoneme in one session, from before Sprint 3. Nothing in the current pipeline writes these anymore; kept for backward compatibility, not part of the primary flow |

### Full property schema

Every property, its type, and whether it's guaranteed to be set. Use this when writing your own Cypher instead of the Python helpers below — `null` handling matters (e.g. `AVG()` skips nulls, but string-typed nulls or missing keys will error).

**`User`**

| Property | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `user_id` | string | yes | Primary key. Format: `"whatsapp:+16085551234"` — always include the `whatsapp:` prefix so every layer matches on the same key |
| `phone_number` | string | yes | Same number, without the `whatsapp:` prefix. (There's an open TODO in `knowledge_graph.py` — `#change phone to email, remove agegroup` — not yet applied. If you make that change, `onboarding_survey.py`'s `create_user(phone_number=..., age_group=...)` call and this doc both need updating in the same commit, or onboarding breaks immediately.) |
| `age_group` | string | yes | e.g. `"adult"`, `"child"` — see the TODO note above |
| `native_language` | string | yes | e.g. `"English"` |
| `created_at` | integer | yes | Epoch millis, set automatically by `create_user()` — never pass this in yourself |

**`Track`** (only as many nodes as `seed_tracks()` defines — currently 2, see below)

| Property | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `track_id` | string | yes | Must match `exercise_bank_speech_language.json`'s `"track"` field exactly |
| `name` | string | yes | Human-readable description |

**`Session`**

| Property | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `session_id` | string | yes | Unique per session — caller generates this (e.g. `uuid4()`) |
| `overall_score` | float | **no** | Legacy pre-Sprint-3 field. Pass `None`/omit for new sessions — read `Attempt.score` per question instead, or average them yourself if you need a session-level number |
| `duration_seconds` | integer | yes | Total session length |
| `speech_rate_wpm` | float | **no** | Legacy — per-question rate now lives on `Attempt` |
| `filler_total` | integer | **no** | Legacy — per-question filler count now lives on `Attempt` |
| `embedding` | list\<float\> | **no** | Legacy — embeddings now live on `Attempt`, one per question response, not one per session |
| `timestamp` | integer | yes | Epoch millis, set automatically by `log_session()` |

**`Attempt`** (new in Sprint 3 — one per question/exercise response)

| Property | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `attempt_id` | string | yes | Unique per attempt. Auto-generated by `log_attempt()` if you don't pass one (`{session_id}_attempt_{random}`) |
| `user_id` | string | yes | Duplicated from the parent session/user for query convenience — you can filter attempts by user without a graph traversal |
| `session_id` | string | yes | Which session this question was answered in |
| `exercise_id` | string | yes | Matches an `"id"` in `exercise_bank_speech_language.json`, e.g. `"LAN-EXP-SPK-001"` |
| `subcategory` | string | yes | Matches that exercise's `"subcategory"`, e.g. `"Expressive - Spoken"` |
| `transcription` | string | yes | Whisper's transcription of the response |
| `speech_rate_wpm` | float | **no** | From Whisper analysis |
| `filler_words` | string (JSON) | **no** | **Stored as a JSON string, not a native map** — Neo4j node properties can only be primitives or arrays of primitives, never nested objects. Originally a dict like `{"um": 2, "uh": 1}`; read it back with `json.loads(...)` |
| `filler_total` | integer | **no** | From Whisper analysis |
| `total_duration_s` | float | **no** | Length of this one response, in seconds |
| `score` | float | yes | 0.0–1.0, from the track-specific scorer (`track_result["score"]`) |
| `scoring_method` | string | yes | Which scorer produced `score`, e.g. `"cnn_phoneme_v1"` — tracks can use different scoring methods, so don't assume they're comparable across `subcategory` values |
| `scoring_details` | string (JSON) | **no** | **Also JSON-serialized**, same reason as `filler_words`. Whatever extra detail the scorer returned (`track_result.get("details", {})`) |
| `weak_phonemes` | list\<string\> | **no** | Phonemes flagged weak in this specific response, e.g. `["/r/", "/th/"]`. Stored as a plain list property (cheap direct read) **and** as `Attempt-[:WEAK_AT]->Phoneme` edges (graph traversal) — both represent the same data, use whichever is more convenient |
| `embedding` | list\<float\> | **no** | wav2vec vector for this one response. This is where DTW/cosine comparison now reads embeddings from — `Session.embedding` is legacy and no longer populated by the current pipeline |
| `timestamp` | integer | yes | Epoch millis, set automatically by `log_attempt()` |

**`Phoneme`**

| Property | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `symbol` | string | yes | e.g. `"/r/"`, `"/th/"`, `"/s/"` — one node per distinct symbol, reused (`MERGE`d) across all users/attempts |

**`Score`** (legacy — see Node types table above)

| Property | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `value` | float | yes | 0.0–1.0. Must be numeric, not a string — `AVG()` throws a type error on strings |
| `timestamp` | integer | yes | Epoch millis, set automatically by `log_phoneme_score()` |

### Relationships

| Relationship | From → To | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `ASSIGNED_TO` | `User → Track` | Which therapy track this user is on |
| `HAS_SESSION` | `User → Session` | Links a user to all their sessions |
| `HAS_ATTEMPT` | `Session → Attempt` | **New in Sprint 3.** Links a session to each question answered within it |
| `WEAK_AT` (from `Attempt`) | `Attempt → Phoneme` | **New in Sprint 3.** Phonemes flagged weak in this one question response |
| `WEAK_AT` (from `User`) | `User → Phoneme` | Phonemes flagged weak in at least `min_occurrences` of the user's attempts overall — see `update_weak_phonemes()` below. Same relationship type as the `Attempt`-level edge, different starting node — check which node your query starts from |
| `CONTAINS_SCORE` | `Session → Score` | Legacy — links a session to an old-style averaged phoneme score |
| `FOR_PHONEME` | `Score → Phoneme` | Legacy — which phoneme a legacy `Score` belongs to |

### Visual overview

```
(User)-[:ASSIGNED_TO]->(Track)
(User)-[:HAS_SESSION]->(Session)
(Session)-[:HAS_ATTEMPT]->(Attempt)
(Attempt)-[:WEAK_AT]->(Phoneme)
(User)-[:WEAK_AT]->(Phoneme)                  # rolled up from Attempt-level WEAK_AT edges

# legacy, pre-Sprint-3, nothing currently writes these:
(Session)-[:CONTAINS_SCORE]->(Score)
(Score)-[:FOR_PHONEME]->(Phoneme)
```

